§ `s 5 and s 4 -- am I ordinarily resident, am I a foreign person`

#ASSERT `Am I ordinarily resident in Australia` `Priya, a permanent resident living in Perth` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I ordinarily resident in Australia` `Priya, a permanent resident who arrived 120 days ago` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I ordinarily resident in Australia` `Daniel, a citizen living in Perth` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I ordinarily resident in Australia` `Mei, on a four-year temporary visa, 300 days here` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I ordinarily resident in Australia` `Aroha, a New Zealand citizen on a special category visa, 250 days here` EQUALS TRUE

#ASSERT `Am I a foreign person` `Priya, a permanent resident living in Perth` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a foreign person` `Daniel, a citizen living in Perth` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a foreign person` `Priya, a permanent resident who arrived 120 days ago` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a foreign person` `a citizen living in Singapore` EQUALS TRUE

#ASSERT `Am I a temporary resident` `Mei, on a four-year temporary visa, 300 days here` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a temporary resident` `Arjun, on a bridging visa awaiting his permanent visa` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a temporary resident` `Hans, overseas on a short visitor visa` EQUALS FALSE

§ `s 4, s 12, s 52 -- the land, the interest, the dwelling, the threshold`

#ASSERT `Is it residential land` `a vacant block that could take 2 dwellings, bought alone` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it residential land` `a vacant site that could take 12 dwellings, bought alone` EQUALS FALSE

#ASSERT `Am I acquiring an interest in Australian land` `a 3-year lease of the apartment` EQUALS FALSE

#ASSERT `Is it an established dwelling` `d037: the East Perth apartment, joint tenants with Daniel` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it an established dwelling` `a new apartment from the developer, never occupied, bought alone` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is it an established dwelling` `a developer's apartment occupied 14 months, bought alone` EQUALS TRUE

#ASSERT `Is the threshold test met` `d037: the East Perth apartment, joint tenants with Daniel` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the threshold test met` `a shopping centre with a flat, under the reg 52(5) threshold` EQUALS FALSE

§ `Regulation ss 35, 38 -- the exemptions`

#ASSERT `Which exemption applies to me` `Priya, a permanent resident who arrived 120 days ago` `d037: the East Perth apartment, joint tenants with Daniel` EQUALS `reg 38(2)(a): the holder of a permanent visa`
#ASSERT `Which exemption applies to me` `Aroha, a New Zealand citizen on a special category visa, 100 days here` `d037 variant: the same apartment bought alone` EQUALS `reg 38(2)(b): the holder of a special category visa`
#ASSERT `Which exemption applies to me` `a citizen living in Singapore` `d037 variant: the same apartment bought alone` EQUALS `reg 35(1)(a): an Australian citizen not ordinarily resident in Australia`
#ASSERT `Which exemption applies to me` `Mei, on a four-year temporary visa, 300 days here` `d037: the East Perth apartment, joint tenants with Daniel` EQUALS `reg 38(3): joint tenants with a spouse or partner who is a citizen or holds a permanent or special category visa`
#ASSERT `Which exemption applies to me` `Mei, on a four-year temporary visa, 300 days here` `d037 variant: the same apartment as tenants in common with Daniel` EQUALS `no exemption applies`
#ASSERT `Which exemption applies to me` `Hans, overseas on a short visitor visa` `d037 variant: joint tenants with Mei, a temporary visa holder` EQUALS `no exemption applies`

